                "headline": "Marine Weather Statement issued October 31 at 9:18AM PDT by NWS Los Angeles/Oxnard CA",
                "description": "Scattered showers will continue across the coastal waters through\nSunday morning. With increasing instability and enhanced potential\nfor rotating storms, isolated waterspouts will be possible today,\nmainly from the coastal waters off of the Santa Barbara Central\nCoast southward to the inner waters south of Point Conception.\nThese same areas will also have a 5-10 percent chance of\nthunderstorms today.\n\nWaterspouts are dangerous and can capsize boats. Never move\ncloser to investigate or take photos. The best way to avoid a\nwaterspout is to move at a 90 degree angle to its apparent\nmovement.",
